--!strict
-- The loading card (docs/ARCHITECTURE.md 8.0, GAME_DESIGN 11): Driftling Isle at dusk over the whole screen from the
-- client's first frame until the first picture of the island is on screen, then it fades into it.
--
-- The user asked for it: "the loading screen isnt centered ... can you also make the loading screen more detailed, like
-- the bakery game, with baked in models and animations?" (2026-11-12). Before, a flat sea-blue curtain with the title
-- laid out at the screen's size when it was made (stale on a window still settling, so it sat off centre).
--
-- Who drives it
-- * ReplicatedFirst.Loading.Boot (a LocalScript that runs before the rest of the game has arrived) puts it up with
--   LoadingCard.show() as its first act and removes Roblox's own loading screen.
-- * The client's Main calls show() on its first line too (nothing when Boot has), moves it through its phases and
--   reports the first picture's progress; finish() once the picture is on screen fills the bar, fades the card out
--   (FADE_SEC, in FADE_STEPS steps) and destroys it. Past SAFETY_SEC it goes by itself.
--
-- What it shows (UI px on a pixel canvas: K screen px each, the game's own pixel size: 2 on a phone, 3 at 1080p), laid
-- out from the canvas's size every time it changes (never a size taken once):
-- * painted into one image: a dusk sky in dithered bands with stars, the sun going down on the horizon with far islands
--   either side, a banded sea with the sun's path on it and small waves, and in the middle the island: its shallows, a
--   ring of foam, wet sand, the sand with its cliff in front, the grass, a patch of sand round the campfire;
-- * on it the game's own models, drawn ahead of time (src/first/LoadingArt, generated by tools/preview/loading_art.sh
--   through Pixel/Snapshot): three palms, a Grass Hut, a Tent, Tiki Torches, Flower Beds and Round Bushes, the wild Tide
--   Pool blinking,
--   the campfire flickering and throwing embers, a villager cheering by it; two villagers strolling up and down the
--   island with a Mossbun and a Clawdle at their heels, a Gullfin hopping along the front; the expedition boat rocking
--   past out at sea, gulls crossing the sky, stars twinkling, wave crests and glints of sun coming and going;
-- * over the sky, centred: "Driftling Isle" in the pixel font's big face (gold, the title's ink outline), a short
--   status that follows the real phases, a progress bar in a frame of planks, and at the foot a tip on an ink plate.
-- Sprites are ImageLabels on the decoded atlas (one EditableImage), moved from one Heartbeat at most SCENE_FPS times a
-- second, at whole UI px. Without EditableImages the card is a plain one: the sky, the sea, the title and the bar.
--
-- Nothing from ReplicatedStorage at load (Boot runs before it has arrived): the colours are the palette's written out,
-- and the pixel font (Render/PixelFont, PixelFontData) is mapped beside this module.
--
-- API (client only)
--   LoadingCard.show()           puts the card up (once)
--   LoadingCard.phase(name)      "island" (waiting for the island) | "picture" (drawing it)
--   LoadingCard.progress(f)      the first picture's progress, 0..1 (phase "picture")
--   LoadingCard.finish()         the first picture is on screen: fill, fade out, destroy (once)
--   LoadingCard.state()          for the sims: { up, phase, bar, finished, fading, painted, fallback, actors, ticks, K,
--                                size, title (its rect: { x0, y0, x1, y1 }, UI px), island ({ cx, cy, rx, ry }) }
